---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const greetz =
  'GREETZ TO: everyone still hand-writing HTML  ::  16colo.rs  ::  textfiles.com  ::  wiby.me  ::  512kb.club  ::  neocities  ::  the small web  ::  and you, reading the source  ::  ';
---
<Base title={'demo \u2014 TinkSoft'} description="A pure-CSS demoscene demo part.">
  <header class="demo-head scene-panel">
    <p class="scene-label">[DEMO PARTS]</p>
    <p class="eyebrow">PUBLIC NODE // CSS ONLY</p>
    <h1>demo</h1>
    <p>Three little scene parts, rendered by the browser and nothing else.</p>
  </header>

  <div class="parts">
    <section class="scene-panel">
      <p class="scene-label">[01 // RASTER]</p>
      <div class="bars" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <h2>raster / copper bars</h2>
      <p>Repeating color bands slide across a fixed strip, like a scanline-era copper effect.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="scene-panel">
      <p class="scene-label">[02 // PLASMA]</p>
      <div class="plasma" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <h2>plasma field</h2>
      <p>Four translucent radial gradients drift at different speeds and directions until their colors interfere.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="scene-panel">
      <p class="scene-label">[03 // GREETZ]</p>
      <div class="scroller" aria-hidden="true">
        <span class="scroller-strip">{greetz}<span class="scroller-copy">{greetz}</span></span>
      </div>
      <h2>greetz scroller</h2>
      <p>A duplicated inline strip travels left so the loop can return without a seam.</p>
    </section>
  </div>

  <section class="explanation scene-panel">
    <p class="scene-label">[SOURCE NOTES]</p>
    <h2>how the parts work</h2>
    <p>
      This is plain CSS: gradients provide the pixels and keyframes provide the
      motion. There are 0 bytes of JavaScript in this page or anywhere else on
      the site.
    </p>
    <h3>small signal, no payload</h3>
    <p>
      The demo costs only the page's own CSS. The bars repeat a linear gradient,
      the plasma layers combine radial gradients, and the scroller moves an
      inline-block with <code>transform</code>. No canvas, image, library, or
      external font is needed.
    </p>
    <h3>respect the terminal operator</h3>
    <p>
      Under <code>prefers-reduced-motion: reduce</code>, every animation stops.
      The bars and plasma remain in a readable static frame, while the scroller
      stays at the start of its text instead of leaving an empty track. The
      layout also stays usable at the existing 30rem mobile breakpoint.
    </p>
  </section>

  <style>
    .demo-head { margin-bottom: 2rem; border-left: 4px solid var(--accent); }
    .demo-head h1 { margin: 0.25rem 0; }
    .demo-head > p:last-child { margin: 0; color: var(--muted); }
    .parts { display: grid; gap: 1.25rem; }
    .parts .scene-panel { overflow: hidden; }
    .parts h2, .explanation h2 { margin: 1.25rem 0 0.35rem; font-size: 1.05rem; }
    .parts p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; color: var(--muted); }
    .bars {
      height: 5rem;
      border: 1px solid var(--frame);
      background: repeating-linear-gradient(
        0deg,
        color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, var(--ink)) 0 0.12rem,
        var(--accent) 0.12rem 0.33rem,
        color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, var(--ink)) 0.33rem 0.45rem,
        color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent-2) 55%, var(--ink)) 0.45rem 0.57rem,
        var(--accent-2) 0.57rem 0.78rem,
        color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent-2) 55%, var(--ink)) 0.78rem 0.9rem,
        color-mix(in srgb, var(--hot) 55%, var(--ink)) 0.9rem 1.02rem,
        var(--hot) 1.02rem 1.23rem,
        color-mix(in srgb, var(--hot) 55%, var(--ink)) 1.23rem 1.35rem,
        var(--panel) 1.35rem 1.5rem
      );
      background-size: 100% 6rem;
      animation: bars 4s linear infinite;
    }
    .plasma {
      position: relative;
      height: 10rem;
      overflow: hidden;
      border: 1px solid var(--frame);
      background-color: var(--code-bg);
      background-image:
        radial-gradient(circle at 20% 35%, var(--accent) 0 7%, transparent 42%),
        radial-gradient(circle at 80% 65%, var(--accent-2) 0 9%, transparent 46%),
        radial-gradient(circle at 50% 50%, var(--hot) 0 6%, transparent 40%);
      background-size: 52% 68%, 64% 58%, 45% 75%;
      background-repeat: repeat;
      background-position: 0% 0%, 100% 100%, 50% 50%;
      animation: plasma 17s linear infinite alternate;
    }
    .plasma::before {
      position: absolute;
      inset: -25%;
      background: radial-gradient(circle at 60% 40%, var(--accent) 0 8%, transparent 42%);
      background-size: 58% 72%;
      background-repeat: repeat;
      background-position: 0% 0%;
      content: '';
      opacity: 0.72;
      animation: plasma-glow 11s linear infinite alternate-reverse;
    }
    .scroller {
      overflow: hidden;
      border: 1px solid var(--frame);
      background: var(--code-bg);
      color: var(--code-ink);
      line-height: 1.5;
    }
    .scroller-strip {
      display: inline-block;
      min-width: max-content;
      padding: 0.8rem 0;
      white-space: nowrap;
      animation: scroller 28s linear infinite;
    }
    .scroller-copy { display: inline-block; }
    .explanation { margin-top: 1.25rem; border-left: 4px solid var(--accent-2); }
    .explanation h2 { margin-top: 0.25rem; }
    .explanation h3 { margin-bottom: 0.25rem; }
    .explanation p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
    @keyframes bars {
      to { background-position: 0 6rem; }
    }
    @keyframes plasma {
      to { background-position: 100% 100%, 0% 0%, 100% 50%; }
    }
    @keyframes plasma-glow {
      to { background-position: 100% 100%; }
    }
    @keyframes scroller {
      to { transform: translateX(-50%); }
    }
    @media (max-width: 30rem) {
      .bars { height: 4rem; }
      .plasma { height: 8rem; }
      .scroller-strip { font-size: 0.78rem; }
    }
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
      .bars, .plasma, .plasma::before, .scroller-strip { animation: none; }
    }
  </style>
</Base>
